\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. If I may speak like all men,\cf0 
\par \pard\li180\sl180\slmult0 And in angelic tongues,
\par But my heart is without love,
\par I'm like a bowl of brass,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And like a bell that's ringing
\par But is devoid of life,
\par So useless is my labour,
\par I have laboured in vain.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. And if I am well versed in
\par \pard\li180\sl180\slmult0 Propagating His word,
\par And even, hidden mysteries
\par Get revealed unto me,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par If  I have divine wisdom,
\par And faith abundantly,
\par But have a heart without love,
\par All shall not be of use.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. If I divide possessions
\par \pard\li180\sl180\slmult0  And give them to the poor,
\par If I should burn my body,
\par All without trace of love,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par It shall be of little use,
\par And will end up in vain,
\par It is love that doth render
\par My Christianity whole.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Love never harbours evil,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0 Love is never so pleased,
\par But he is pleased at the truth,
\par It bears trouble and toil,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par It bears faith that is truthful,
\par And tasted faith as well,
\par It has a lot of patience,
\par In all situations
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. But true love is unending,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0 Though all things have an end,
\par For preaching and the gospel,
\par And wisdom have an end,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par When faith becomes reality
\par Love does constant remain,
\par And hope thus becomes realized,
\par Love ever shall remain.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  O Jesus, have my spirit,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0 Fully filled with this love,
\par For virtually I've no love,
\par I'm filled with vanity.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par May my soul be beautified,
\par By making use of love,
\par That I may fully please Thee,
\par \pard      On earth here and above.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

